      },
      {
        "title": "History of the Danner 6490",
        "summary": "Covers the original 6490: a full-leather boot with a steel shank, light for its time, named best-value hiking boot in 1970 amid the outdoor and environmental boom.",
        "first_segment": 1,
        "last_segment": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "One-piece construction and Gore-Tex",
        "summary": "Explains the low-seam, one-piece leather construction and its benefits, and Danner's early adoption of Gore-Tex as the first fully waterproof leather boot.",
        "first_segment": 3,
        "last_segment": 4
      },
      {
        "title": "Sponsor: Saint Bones",
        "summary": "Sponsor read for Saint Bones and their 53 sunglasses with a sterling silver skull.",
