        "last_segment": 6
      },
      {
        "title": "Sole construction and synthetic materials",
        "summary": "Describes the change from a solid rubber sole to a rubber, foam and rubber stack for less weight and more cushion, and why much of the boot is now synthetic.",
        "first_segment": 6,
        "last_segment": 7
      },
      {
        "title": "Tongue design",
        "summary": "Shows the folded, one-sided tongue flap that adds protection and keeps water out, a design attributed to a Paraboot sister company.",
        "first_segment": 7,
        "last_segment": 8
      },
      {
        "title": "Merrell Moab 3 comparison and recraftability",
        "summary": "Lists the Moab 3's advantages over the Danner, then argues Danner's recraftability and its persistence among modern boots in stores make it special.",
        "first_segment": 8,
        "last_segment": 9
      },
      {
        "title": "Gore-Tex and leather water test",
        "summary": "Soaks the boots and explains why Michael dislikes pairing a waterproof membrane with leather, contrasted with the synthetic Moab, where a membrane makes sense.",
